{# Everything search_knowledge_base says back to the model.

   This is the Class B half of prompt routing: instructions that depend on what
   retrieval actually RETURNED, which the system prompt cannot know because it is
   fixed before the tool runs. Each branch below is paid only on the turns where its
   condition is real, which is why the system prompt can stay silent about all of it.

   `outcome` is DECIDED in backend/tools/knowledge.py and merely rendered here. The
   template selects wording; it does not inspect the trace or apply policy. Keep it
   that way — a condition richer than "which outcome" belongs in the tool.

   The sentence lines below run long ON PURPOSE. A model reads what is rendered, not
   the source, and hard-wrapping a sentence here puts real newlines mid-phrase in the
   prompt — extra tokens, and it breaks any downstream match on a phrase that now
   straddles a line break. Let the editor soft-wrap; do not reflow these by hand.

   Whitespace: trim_blocks is on, so the newline after every {% %} tag is swallowed. #}
{% if outcome == "call_limit" %}
TOOL_CALL_LIMIT_REACHED: search_knowledge_base has already been called once in this turn. Use the existing retrieval result and provide the final answer directly.
{% elif outcome == "needs_clarification" %}
NEEDS_CLARIFICATION: {{ prompt }}
Put this question to the user directly. Do not answer from the retrieved context.
{% elif outcome == "needs_scope_selection" %}
NEEDS_SCOPE_SELECTION: {{ prompt }}
{% if options %}
Options: {{ options | join("; ") }}
{% endif %}
Ask the user to choose. Do not answer from the retrieved context.
{% elif outcome == "retrieval_error" %}
RETRIEVAL_ERROR: The knowledge base could not be searched right now due to a temporary technical issue. Tell the user a brief technical problem interrupted the search and to try again in a moment. Do NOT claim the knowledge base lacks this information, and do not answer from your own knowledge.
{% elif outcome == "no_knowledge" %}
NO_KNOWLEDGE: No reliable relevant documents were found in the knowledge base. Tell the user it does not contain reliable information on this, and do not answer from your own knowledge.
{% elif outcome == "empty" %}
No relevant documents found in the knowledge base.
{% else %}
Retrieved Chunks:
{{ chunks }}
{% if rewritten %}

Note: this turn re-queried using a step-back question or a HyDE document. Those are retrieval aids, not evidence — cite only the chunks above.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
